{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_prediction_s93_item3_janak_janak_slater_relation", "label": "Slater/Janak relation dE/df = eps", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S93-ITEM3-JANAK.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "M's s93 ruling re-read the literature and directed testing the identity rather than subdividing further, with Slater (HF, 1972 TS) and Koopmans (1934) attributed. If it holds, relaxation is the f-dependence of the integrand and no relaxation object remains to be named."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_s93_item3_janak_fractional_pair_factor", "label": "Fractional pair factor ceff(f) linear in f", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S93-ITEM3-JANAK.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ceff(f) = [qc(qc-1) + 2 f qc]/(qc+f) makes the shell self-pair energy linear in f, which is what forces the extra qc(1-f)/(qc+f) U_cc term beside eps_c; dropping it is can-fail A, expected to miss by 0.05-0.1 Ha."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_s93_item3_janak_gauss_legendre_integral", "label": "Five-point Gauss-Legendre occupation integral", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S93-ITEM3-JANAK.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every node is a full SCF solve and the nodes sweep the open interval (0,1) so the shell is present at every node; the identity is exact by Hellmann-Feynman in f and only quadrature error remains."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_s93_item3_janak_u_cc", "label": "Own-shell pair interaction U_cc", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-S93-ITEM3-JANAK.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "recovered_prediction_s93_ite